SWEET AUDIO POLISH (patch 0394, plan A12 polish), on top of 0393. User decision 2026-11-18 (speed first, loudness first):
- /dev/sweetaudio gain: default -6 dB (was -15), max 0 dB (was -6); every sample is clamped at -3 dBFS (23197) after the gain, so no gain
  setting drives the amps (DSP bypassed) above -3 dBFS. The level make-up for quiet iOS mixes is done in userland (libsalog tap limiter).
- The sweetaoc=15 boot self-test (2 beeps) is opt-in: boot-arg sweetaudiotest=1; without it /dev/sweetaudio opens right away, silent boot.
- sweetaoc=15 implies sweetamp=1 (the amp windows / identify run) when sweetamp is not given.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_amp.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_amp.c
index 49e4c7a..fad7d8f 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_amp.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_amp.c
@@ -126,7 +126,12 @@ sweet_amp_init(void)
 		return;
 	}
 	started = 1;
-	if (!PE_parse_boot_argn("sweetamp", &on, sizeof(on)) || on == 0) {
+	if (!PE_parse_boot_argn("sweetamp", &on, sizeof(on))) {
+		uint32_t aoc = 0;       /* patch 0394: sweetaoc=15 (/dev/sweetaudio) implies sweetamp=1 */
+
+		on = PE_parse_boot_argn("sweetaoc", &aoc, sizeof(aoc)) && aoc == 15u ? 1u : 0u;
+	}
+	if (on == 0) {
 		return;         /* default: no map, no read */
 	}
 	if (on != 1) {
